# Local ATP Benchmark

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"},
  {:table, "0.1.2"},
  # {:atp_benchmark_runner, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__), force: true}
  {:atp_benchmark_runner, github: "penthooose/atp_benchmark_runner", force: true}

])
```

## 1. Configuration — local storage

All benchmark data lives in `./tmp/` by default. Override via environment
variables (`ATP_BENCHMARK_RUNNER_STORE_DIR`, `ATP_BENCHMARK_RUNNER_TPTP_DIR`,
`ATP_BENCHMARK_RUNNER_SMT_TMP_DIR`) or pass `:dir`/`:root_dir` options to
individual API functions.

```elixir
IO.puts("Store directory:   #{AtpBenchmarkRunner.store_dir()}")
IO.puts("TPTP directory:    #{AtpBenchmarkRunner.tptp_dir()}")
IO.puts("SMT temp dir:      #{AtpBenchmarkRunner.Config.smt_tmp_dir()}")
```

## 2. Point to your TPTP library

Set `ATP_BENCHMARK_RUNNER_TPTP_DIR` or adjust the path below to your
downloaded TPTP archive.

```elixir
# Already downloaded? Uncomment and set the path to skip the download step:
# System.put_env("ATP_BENCHMARK_RUNNER_TPTP_DIR", "C:/Users/Paul/.../tmp/tptp")

tptp_lib = AtpBenchmarkRunner.TPTP.library_root(root_dir: AtpBenchmarkRunner.tptp_dir())
IO.puts("TPTP library root: #{tptp_lib}")
IO.puts("Problems directory exists: #{File.dir?(Path.join(tptp_lib, "Problems"))}")
```

## 3. Download TPTP from tptp.org (optional — skip if already downloaded)

```elixir
# Download and extract the official TPTP archive (∼881MB, expands to ∼9.9GB).
# Skip this if you already have it (see step 2).

archive = AtpBenchmarkRunner.ensure_tptp_archive(
  root_dir: AtpBenchmarkRunner.tptp_dir(),
  force: false
)

case archive do
  {:ok, path} ->
    IO.puts("TPTP archive ready at: #{path}")
  {:error, reason} ->
    IO.puts("Download skipped or failed: #{inspect(reason)}")
    IO.puts("(This is fine if you already have it — see step 2)")
end
```

## 4. Detect available execution methods

```elixir
avail = AtpBenchmarkRunner.LocalRunner.detect_available()
```

## 5. Pre-build container images

Missing images are also automatically built / pulled when `auto_ensure_images: true` is
set in step 8.

```elixir
build_provers = [:eprover, :vampire, :cvc5, :zipperposition, :leo3]

IO.puts("Pre-building container images for: #{inspect(build_provers)}")
Enum.each(build_provers, fn name ->
  case AtpBenchmarkRunner.LocalRunner.docker_image_status(name) do
    :available -> IO.puts("  #{name} already available")
    _ ->
      try do
        IO.puts(" #{name}...")
        AtpBenchmarkRunner.LocalRunner.ensure_docker_image!(name)
      rescue
        e -> IO.puts("  #{String.slice(Exception.message(e), 0, 200)}")
      end
  end
end)
```

---

## 6. Select benchmark problems

Pass a plain list of TPTP filenames (no keyword wrapper needed). Falls back
to bundled `priv/tptp_examples` when no full archive is available.

> **TPTP naming:** `ANA002-4.p` — the `-4` is a _version number_, not a
> difficulty rating. Actual difficulty is the `Rating:` field (0.00–1.00) in
> each problem's TPTP header comments.

```elixir
problems = AtpBenchmarkRunner.select_problems([
  "ALG001+0.p",
  "GRP001-0.p",
  "GRP002+0.p",
  "GRP003+0.p",
  "GRP004+0.p",
  "LAT001+0.p",
  "PUZ001+0.p",
  "REL001+0.p",
  "SET001^0.p",
  "SYN000+0.p",
  "THF001+0.p"
])

IO.puts("Loaded #{length(problems)} problem(s):\n")

header = "| Name | Domain | Logic | Rating | Expected |"
sep    = "|------|--------|-------|--------|----------|"

IO.puts(header)
IO.puts(sep)

Enum.each(problems, fn p ->
  IO.puts("| #{p.name} | #{p.domain || "?"} | #{p.logic || "?"} | #{p.rating} | #{p.expected_status || "?"} |")
end)

# Show a summary
summary = AtpBenchmarkRunner.TPTP.summarize(problems)
IO.puts("")
IO.puts("Summary: #{summary.count} problems loaded")
```

---

## 7. Select provers for local execution

```elixir
selected_provers = [
  # :tableaux,
  :eprover,
  :vampire,
  :cvc5,
  :zipperposition,
  :leo3,
  # :leo2,
  # :lash
]

IO.puts("Selected #{length(selected_provers)} prover(s):")
Enum.each(selected_provers, fn name ->
  IO.puts("  - #{AtpBenchmarkRunner.Prover.builtin!(name).label}")
end)
```

---

## 8. Bootstrap & run benchmark

`bootstrap/3` creates a plan (`Run` struct). `run_benchmark/1` executes it.

```elixir
plan = AtpBenchmarkRunner.bootstrap(selected_provers, problems,
  mode: :local,
  timeout_seconds: 120,
  auto_ensure_images: true
)

results = AtpBenchmarkRunner.run_benchmark(plan)
```

HPC mode stub

```elixir
# session = HpcConnect.Session.local()
# plan = AtpBenchmarkRunner.bootstrap(session, selected_provers, problems,
#   mode: :hpc,
#   hpc_mode: :single_node,  # or :multi_node
#   timeout_seconds: 120
# )
# results = AtpBenchmarkRunner.run_benchmark(plan)
```

---

## 9. Prover Results

```elixir
AtpBenchmarkRunner.results_table(results)
```

### Full details with proofs

```elixir
AtpBenchmarkRunner.explain_full(results) |> IO.puts()
```

### Filter by prover

```elixir
target_prover = :leo3

AtpBenchmarkRunner.verbose_report(results, prover: target_prover, solved_only: true)
|> Enum.each(&IO.puts/1)
```

### View a full proof

```elixir
AtpBenchmarkRunner.show_proof(results, :vampire, "GRP001-0")
```

### Raw Prover Debug Output

```elixir
target_prover = :vampire
target_problem = "GRP001-0"

result = Enum.find(results, fn r ->
  r.prover == target_prover and r.problem_id == target_problem
end)

if result && result.raw_output do
  IO.puts("Raw output for #{result.problem_id} / #{result.prover}:")
  IO.puts("")
  IO.puts(result.raw_output)
else
  IO.puts("Result not found or no raw output stored (rerun with include_raw_output: true)")
end
```

---

## 10. Convert TPTP to SMT-LIB (for SMT-based provers like CVC5)

Some provers (notably CVC5's static binary) do not natively parse TPTP and
require SMT-LIB input. The runner handles this automatically during execution,
but you can also convert files manually:

```elixir
# Pick one of the bundled examples as a test case
example_p = AtpBenchmarkRunner.install_tptp_examples!() |> List.first()

IO.puts("Converting: #{example_p}")

# Convert to SMT-LIB string
smt_content = AtpBenchmarkRunner.convert_tptp_to_smt!(example_p)
IO.puts("SMT-LIB output (#{String.length(smt_content)} chars):\n")
IO.puts(String.slice(smt_content, 0, 500) <> "\n...")

# Or write to the configured temp directory and get the path back
smt_path = AtpBenchmarkRunner.convert_tptp_to_smt_path!(example_p)
IO.puts("\nWritten to: #{smt_path}")
```

The temp directory is configurable via `ATP_BENCHMARK_RUNNER_SMT_TMP_DIR` env var
or `AtpBenchmarkRunner.Config.smt_tmp_dir/1`.

---

## 11. Aggregated report

```elixir
report = AtpBenchmarkRunner.report(results)

IO.puts("Run ID: #{report.run_id}")
IO.puts("Generated: #{report.generated_at}\n")
IO.puts(report.markdown)
```

### Per-prover breakdown

```elixir
AtpBenchmarkRunner.print_per_prover(report)
```

### Per-problem comparison

```elixir
AtpBenchmarkRunner.print_per_problem(report)
```

---

## 12. Persist results to local store

```elixir
run = AtpBenchmarkRunner.new_run(
  title: "Local smoke test",
  problems: problems,
  provers: selected_provers,
  walltime: "00:30:00",
  problem_timeout_seconds: 30
)

run_path = AtpBenchmarkRunner.save_run!(run)
IO.puts("Run saved: #{run_path}")

results_path = AtpBenchmarkRunner.save_results!(run, results)
IO.puts("Results saved: #{results_path}")

report_path = AtpBenchmarkRunner.save_report!(run, report)
IO.puts("Report saved: #{report_path}")
```

---

## 13. Compare with a previous run (longitudinal diff)

```elixir
prev_results_path = nil

if prev_results_path && File.exists?(prev_results_path) do
  prev_results = AtpBenchmarkRunner.Store.load_results!(prev_results_path)
  diff = AtpBenchmarkRunner.compare_runs(prev_results, results)
  IO.puts(AtpBenchmarkRunner.diff_markdown(diff))
else
  IO.puts("No previous results to compare against")
end
```
